// kldload APT post-transaction snapshot hook.
//
// Role:     snapshot the root dataset AFTER a dpkg transaction, so the pair
//           of apt-pre/apt-post snapshots brackets exactly what changed.
// Read by:  apt(8), after every dpkg run. Placed at
//           /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/00-kldload-snapshot-post.
// Missing:  the pre snapshot still exists, so rollback still works; what is
//           lost is the "after" half, which is what makes a diff possible.
//
// Same `||` as the pre hook, for the same reason and then one more: a
// Post-Invoke that fails makes apt report the transaction as failed AFTER the
// packages are already installed. That is the worst of both — the change
// landed, and every script reading apt's exit status believes it did not.
// See 00-kldload-snapshot-pre for the incident and the policy.

DPkg::Post-Invoke {"/usr/local/sbin/snapshot-create.sh apt-post || { echo 'kldload: WARNING — post-transaction snapshot FAILED; the packages are installed regardless.' >&2; echo 'kldload: see /var/log/kldload/snapshots.log' >&2; }";};
